  "findings": [
    "Source audit supports the narrow separation: SequenceDiagram.addMessage attaches pending CREATE to compatible MessageExo and clears it; DrawableSetInitializer dispatches Step1MessageExo, and CommunicationExoTile performs addStepForLivebox without CommunicationTile.goCreate or ordinary inline-head painting. Rust sequence_ordinary_creation_messages filters only external border topology; sequence_create_attachments and TeozHistory preserve raw CREATE ownership. No missing-target guard, dropped owner, fixture label branch, unexplained new numeric constant or coordinate compensation was introduced.",
    "Whole fresh outputs still refute mechanism acceptance: 19/30 valid cases match, 9 render mismatching SVG, and 2 valid short incoming ? arrows are parse-rejected, in 32 entries including 2 Java-invalid outgoing returns. All 12 old outgoing renderer panics in this fresh cohort disappear; no new pass loss or valid-input error was introduced by this packet.",
    "External note counterexamples lose outbound annotation in both engines. AST has one Create and two Message events but no Note, whereas Java Step1MessageExo creates each NoteBox. Rust try_external_message does not update last_message; try_note sees no owner and returns without emitting the bare note. This parser defect is unchanged by the packet; it is a causal residual, not an introduced regression.",
    "Short ? arrows are accepted by CommandExoArrowLeft/Right and marked short by CommandExoArrowAny.isShortArrow. Rust external regexes accept only square borders. Incoming short-arrow statements disappear, so the later ordinary message is checked against the pending CREATE and rejected. Outgoing short arrows disappear and lose the near label. These errors predate the packet.",
    "Legacy activation and activated-return cases retain all labels but activation bars begin 10 units early; Teoz counterparts match. Fresh group cases fail in both engines and nested group/alt fails in legacy. Existing group/box residuals remain explicit; no envelope/activation ownership repair is claimed here.",
    "Repeated external CREATE witness retains 3 Create and 4 Message events, two labels per participant and 2 lifelines, matching Java. The external-then-different-ordinary witness retains 2 Create and 3 Message events, two labels per each of 3 participants and 3 lifelines. Both engines match. The independent ordinary creation/destroy control matches both revisions. TeozHistory source keeps the external raw owner and the existing ownership unit passes; this is bounded support, not whole acceptance.",
    "Both outgoing return controls were intended valid but Java emits Nowhere to return to error pages and stderr. CommandReturn requires an activating message for MessageExo; fallback requires ordinary Message. Their original intent is preserved, observed validity is false, and Rust rejects both before and after."
  ],
